id: pm-rust-oracle-1118
title: Refresh published pm-cli oracle to 2026.11.18
description: "Classify the published CLI divergences, update native parity and validate the locked npm oracle on Linux."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rust#176",oracle
created_at: "2026-11-18T09:41:09.150Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-18T10:53:51.282Z"
author: codex-sol
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-18T09:41:20.010Z",codex-sol,Started from the Dependabot head. npm latest is 2026.11.18. Reviewing the failed matrix and reproducing against the current pin.
  "2026-11-18T09:57:01.888Z",codex-sol,"All seven failed jobs in run 44015087729 report two cases. GH-1707 in 2026.11.13 introduces credential-bearing identity admission and stored-holder redaction. Direct 2026.11.18 probes confirm stored holders are redacted without requiring credential restoration from a clean invocation. The full Linux run also confirms GH-1684 and GH-1703 in 2026.11.14 change TOON receipts and budgeted row counts, and GH-1336 in 2026.11.16 adds claim activity evidence. Implementing these wire changes while the remaining suites run."
  "2026-11-18T10:10:24.585Z",codex-sol,"Published 2026.11.18 accepts the unchanged replay at the old TOON overhead boundary. The same stale-output-cursor defect remains at an adjacent second-projection boundary, with successful replay on either side. Saved an upstream draft after checking related issues. Native already had this stale replay behavior. Kept the existing reprojected-snapshot test and tracked the separate GH-1336 takeover and next write/read work under pm-rust-stale-claim-takeover."
  "2026-11-18T10:15:01.342Z",codex-sol,"GH-1706 in 2026.11.14 is another intended change exposed past the original CI stop. Published CLI probes confirm automatic expired session-lease reclamation and stale_lock_requires_override for a retained item lease. Adopted typed lock guidance and post-commit attribution warnings, plus the GH-1724 nonzero context ownership and idle counts."
  "2026-11-18T10:16:23.222Z",codex-sol,The current Linux format and all-target Clippy gates pass. The published .18 stored-holder comparison and the updated TOON budget and continuation boundary cases passed their focused runs. The full Linux and ownership matrix runs are in progress. Opening the superseding PR as a draft while those gates complete.
  "2026-11-18T10:26:43.095Z",codex-sol,"Opened draft PR 181 at 9ac32be. Its first CI run passed tracker policy, release quality and quick crash checks. Quick Rust identified the outdated release-I/O assertion and context advisory alias mismatch. Both are corrected. The published claim/holder/session lease focused cases passed 3 of 3, the advisory alias oracle test passed, and all 20 refusal unit tests passed. The native list now reconstructs its second projection to replay the emitted cursor; the regression test verifies that changing the source still refuses."
  "2026-11-18T10:50:00.886Z",codex-sol,"At 6920d21, the local Linux unit suites passed all 458 library and 83 CLI tests. The next CI run exposed a context budget mismatch and one optional usage-feedback warning in the ownership fixture. The documented 2026.11.14 UTF-16 compaction suffix now matches the published context output at budgets 100, 1000 and 1200, and the real-copy oracle test passed. The mutation fixture disables unrelated usage feedback. The 2026.11.12 GH-1700 and 2026.11.14 GH-1716 linked-test and artifact receipts and note policy are implemented, with six direct published file comparisons and four focused unit and oracle regressions passing."
  "2026-11-18T10:53:45.626Z",codex-sol,"The native linked-test removal receipt now matches the published CLI byte for byte. The focused SDK linked-note refusal test verifies both authoritative files stay byte-identical and confirms explicit append returns only the edited link. Formatting, Clippy and the focused context and list cursor checks pass. The all-target Linux and broad collection runs remain in progress. PR 154 depends on these overlapping changes landing first."
files[8]{path,scope}:
  src/collections.rs,project
  src/mutation/claim_activity.rs,project
  src/ownership.rs,project
  src/read_output.rs,project
  src/toon_output.rs,project
  tests/claim_release_differential.rs,project
  tests/oracle/package-lock.json,project
  tests/support/mutation_differential.rs,project
tests[3]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  PM_RUST_REQUIRE_PUBLISHED_CLI=1 cargo test --locked --all-targets --all-features --no-fail-fast,project,codex-sol,"2026-11-18T09:58:16.490Z",local_mutation,fix/oracle-pm-cli-1118
  cargo fmt --all -- --check,project,codex-sol,"2026-11-18T09:58:23.289Z",local_mutation,fix/oracle-pm-cli-1118
  cargo clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings,project,codex-sol,"2026-11-18T10:10:28.550Z",local_mutation,fix/oracle-pm-cli-1118
docs[1]{path,scope}:
  README.md,project
body: ""
